  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "psychology-of-money-s008-p00276",
      "source_en": "On the one hand, people that have been investing through the events of 1987, 2000 and 2008 have experienced a lot of different markets. On the other hand, isn’t it possible that this experience can lead to overconfidence? Failing to admit you’re wrong? Anchoring to previous outcomes? Two dangerous things happen when you rely too heavily on investment history as a guide to what’s going to happen next.",
